            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0420" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Observer on the Rhineland High Commission</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Allen</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Coblenz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-28T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>German custodian of Government property agrees to pay expenses connected American
                    representation High Commission and also past expenses to date. Request
                    disposition of latter funds when received. Reference my former telegram,<anchor
                        n="42" xml:id="d285-f1"/> State Department funds no longer necessary for
                    operation this office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Allen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
